{:edb/db-before-t 1802 :edb/db-after-t 1803 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535115 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:14:45.051Z" 13194139535115 true] [17592186100846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331953 13194139535115 true] [17592186100846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331956 13194139535115 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331939 13194139535115 true] [17592186100848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331946 13194139535115 true] [17592186101116 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535115 true] [17592186101116 1100 "What is the coefficient of $(x + π)^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = \\sin x$ about $x = - π$?" 13194139535115 false] [17592186101116 1100 "What is the coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ about $x=-\\pi ?$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186101116 1145 "The coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-\\pi ).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(-\\pi ),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-\\pi )=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(-\\pi )=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{6}.$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331939 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331940 13194139535115 true] [17592186331939 1089 "q-126359" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331939 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535115 true] [17592186331939 1100 "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}$ about $x=0?$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331939 1113 #uuid "384d449f-273e-593f-9d4d-a9fdf55ff2d4" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331939 1145 "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(1-x)^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{6}{(1-x)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{6}{(1-0)^{4}}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6=1.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $1.$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331941 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331942 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331943 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331944 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331945 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1041 "selection" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331943 13194139535115 true] [17592186331940 1110 #uuid "3cd34680-796d-5b2d-a195-fe32a22dd5ff" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331941 1034 "3" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331941 1111 #uuid "e28d33c6-9b54-5018-8c30-20b4328565a7" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331942 1034 "6" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331942 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331942 1111 #uuid "f64f7624-f5e2-5746-81d4-517943568d06" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331943 1034 "1" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331943 1111 #uuid "377d4d07-1be2-5ae5-a838-0cd5db52bc19" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331944 1034 "-1" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331944 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331944 1111 #uuid "4ab1012d-433c-5c61-b762-c95a6cfddbbd" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331945 1034 "-6" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331945 1111 #uuid "aab72c3b-3e42-516f-81fc-8d253ba110c7" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331946 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331947 13194139535115 true] [17592186331946 1089 "q-15479" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331946 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535115 true] [17592186331946 1100 "What is the coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ about $x=-1?$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331946 1113 #uuid "79a56d13-19ce-5345-b6e6-3de7b06f4714" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331946 1145 "The coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-1).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{24}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(-1),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-1)=-\\frac{24}{(-1)^{5}}=-\\frac{24}{(-1)}=24.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(-1)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot 24=\\frac{24}{6}=4.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ is $4.$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331948 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331949 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331950 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331951 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331952 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1041 "selection" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331952 13194139535115 true] [17592186331947 1110 #uuid "8101ebe3-8ace-5fc9-9b0f-a5d20dd4fce9" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331948 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331948 1111 #uuid "49bce016-19b0-5418-a632-3e4a4a465f6f" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331949 1034 "3" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331949 1111 #uuid "71187d4a-22f1-599d-99ed-a5664a0f98f9" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331950 1034 "-\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331950 1111 #uuid "b42176ef-174e-5805-88ab-84857c192b62" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331951 1034 "8" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331951 1111 #uuid "1f0ca27e-b43a-59d9-b50d-713673aeff1a" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331952 1034 "4" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331952 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331952 1111 #uuid "42273e68-e32b-54b0-b2af-9d895f8d8bcb" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331953 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331954 13194139535115 true] [17592186331953 1089 "q-351859" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331953 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535115 true] [17592186331953 1100 "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)={e}^{-2x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=1-2x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331953 1113 #uuid "783fb36c-345a-5c94-9d91-f565c09ac763" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331953 1145 "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & ={e}^{-0}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-2{e}^{-0}=-2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =4{e}^{-0}=4 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-8{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-8{e}^{-0}=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1-2\\cdot x+4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1-2x+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331955 13194139535115 true] [17592186331954 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535115 true] [17592186331954 1041 "field-1" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331954 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331955 13194139535115 true] [17592186331954 1110 #uuid "f2a61a26-d697-50e5-9a14-f09ca5b0e334" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331955 1034 "2x^2-\\frac{4}{3}x^3" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331955 1111 #uuid "3ba2eba6-98da-551a-a9d7-eaba0126d0c6" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331956 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331957 13194139535115 true] [17592186331956 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331959 13194139535115 true] [17592186331956 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331961 13194139535115 true] [17592186331956 1089 "q-351980" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331956 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535115 true] [17592186331956 1100 "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ about $x=0.$ Do  not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n${x}^{3}$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331956 1113 #uuid "da23cd02-a4af-5514-bd1d-fc11e7c72462" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331956 1145 "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results into our Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x+(-\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{12}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331958 13194139535115 true] [17592186331957 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535115 true] [17592186331957 1041 "field-1" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331957 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331958 13194139535115 true] [17592186331957 1110 #uuid "e10cb6b6-68f5-50a6-9f85-97dc918b5cc0" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331958 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331958 1111 #uuid "fce4228c-cfb9-5019-80e2-cc10096c0284" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331959 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331960 13194139535115 true] [17592186331959 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535115 true] [17592186331959 1041 "field-2" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331959 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331960 13194139535115 true] [17592186331959 1110 #uuid "c856bb87-8e3b-5471-8c50-c413f3aba9de" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331960 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535115 true] [17592186331960 1111 #uuid "55dfc2a7-a4a6-59e8-afc2-ff10a44550da" 13194139535115 true] [17592186331961 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331962 13194139535115 true] [17592186331961 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535115 true] [17